# Every key the app requires, listed here — this file is the single source of truth
# for "what configuration does this project need."
#
# Values are 1Password secret references, not secrets. A reference is just an
# address, so this file is safe to commit and safe for an agent to read.
#
#   op://<vault>/<item>/<field>
#
# ── Running the app ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NFO Hero needs no keys yet, so ./scripts/dev runs without `op`. When the first
# secret lands, add its reference below and wrap the command in ./scripts/dev with
# `op run --env-file=.env.example --`. That script stays the one place the run
# command is written; never copy the longhand into README or AGENTS.md.
#
# Never write a plaintext .env.
#
# `op run` decrypts into the child process's environment, masks any secret that
# reaches stdout, and the values vanish when the process exits. Nothing is ever
# written to disk.
#
# Non-secrets stay literal; only secrets need a reference.
#
# ── Setup ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#   brew install 1password-cli        # then enable Developer → CLI in the app
#   op signin
#   op vault create <project-name>    # one vault per project, so access is scoped
#   op item create --category=login --vault=<project-name> --title='Example API' \
#     credential='<paste>'
#
# Copy a reference straight from the 1Password app: right-click a field →
# "Copy Secret Reference". Verify one with `op read '<ref>'` in your own shell —
# not through an agent, which would capture the plaintext in its transcript.
#
# ── CI ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Create a service account scoped to this project's vault and set OP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_TOKEN
# as the only repo secret. The token authenticates the `op` CLI; it injects nothing on
# its own — CI still has to wrap the step, `op run --env-file=.env.example -- ./scripts/check`,
# with the token in that step's `env:`. See .github/workflows/check.yml. One secret to
# rotate instead of twenty.
#
# ── Without 1Password ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to .env, replace each op:// reference with a real value, and keep
# it untracked (.gitignore already covers it). Weaker: the plaintext lives on disk.
# The key list stays identical either way.
